From 8f2483f3d8eefdf5e8efccbffaec5037f3d34479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:05:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(shared): Profile Q's signer rule (Q4) in the
 signature check (lifecycle Level 3)

SignaturePolicy gains profile_q: the variant (no-root-ecdsa or strict) and
the activation block B_Q that the operators' statements announced. A
verification whose pinned block is at or after B_Q is decided by the
signer's code at that block, whatever the mode:
- no code, or an EIP-7702 indicator: refused, with no ERC-1271 call;
- other code, an EIP-7851 ECDSA-disabled indicator included: ERC-1271
  only, with no fallback, in the no-root-ecdsa variant; refused with no
  call in the strict variant.
E3 signers are accepted by the KDA route, which runs before this check.
H1 caps and H4 attempts still apply. New error ProfileQRefused (final).

tests/profile_q.rs: 10 tests with a mocked provider pinning the RPC
sequence, including the KDA route under both variants.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
